{
  "_comment": [
    "Declared foreground/background pairs that must meet WCAG 2.2 AA in Light and Dark.",
    "Tokens are named as in packages/tokens/io/sync (collection prefix omitted); a bare name resolves in components, then semantic, then primitive.",
    "kind 'text' needs 4.5:1, 'non-text' (icons, indicators, boundaries) needs 3:1. Disabled states are exempt under WCAG and are not declared.",
    "knownFailures is a ratchet: each entry is an accepted failure with a reason. A new failure fails the check; a known failure that starts passing must be removed.",
    "Borders and fills are declared when they are the only visual boundary of a control that has no text label (input, checkbox, radio, switch, slider) and for focus indicators. Controls with a text label (outline button, toggle) are not, because the label identifies them."
  ],
  "thresholds": {
    "text": 4.5,
    "non-text": 3
  },
